                    "**Senior**  \nAt Optima Geeks, I work as a Lead Software Engineer, owning the architecture, development, and delivery of scalable, production-ready AI and full-stack platforms. I lead cross-functional initiatives spanning frontend, backend, AI systems, and cloud infrastructure, with a strong focus on system design, reliability, and long-term scalability. Key Responsibilities & Impact -Led end-to-end architecture and implementation of AI-driven and full-stack platforms in production environments -Designed and deployed agentic and generative AI systems, including LLM workflows, RAG pipelines, and multi-agent architectures -Built scalable agent frameworks using LangChain, LangGraph, CrewAI, and Agno -Drove full-stack development across MERN, including React, Next.js, Node.js, NestJS, Express, Hono, and Deno -Developed high-performance backend and AI microservices using Node.js and Python (FastAPI) -Owned system design and architectural decisions for scalable, fault-tolerant, and secure systems -Designed and operated cloud-native infrastructure using Docker, Kubernetes, and Kafka -Implemented CI/CD pipelines and Infrastructure as Code with Jenkins, Terraform, and Ansible -Deployed and scaled systems across AWS, GCP, and Azure -Ensured performance, reliability, observability, and security across services and data layers -Mentored engineers and partnered with product and leadership teams on technical strategy and roadmap execution\n### Senior Software Engineer at OptimaGeeks (2025-11-01 – 2026-02-01)\n**Senior**  \nAt Optima Geeks, I serve as a Senior Developer specializing in AI model development, multi-agent architectures, and scalable infrastructure. My work spans across both the MERN stack and Python ecosystem, enabling end-to-end AI-powered system design and deployment. *Key Responsibilities -Designing and implementing AI models, LLM-powered workflows, and multi-agent systems. -Building robust agent architectures for automation, reasoning, and complex decision-making pipelines. -Developing and maintaining infrastructure for scalable AI services, including orchestration, cloud deployments, and optimization. -Leading development across the MERN stack (MongoDB, Express, React, Node.js). -Creating backend services, APIs, and AI microservices in Python. -Ensuring reliability, performance, and best practices across AI and software systems. -Mentoring team members and collaborating on product architecture and technical strategy.\nsystems management, core technologies, intelligent process automation, architecture, best practices, secure systems, ai model development, ansible, terraform, ansible, core, architectural design, pipelines, ai cloud, postgresql, product architecture, design, strategy roadmap, cross-functional, smart, systems design, end-to-end, rag, firebase, leadership, data, mern stack development, cloud architecture, software engineering, python, implementation, frontend development, customization, engineer, spanning cloud apps, cloud-native infrastructure, event-driven architectures, full-stack developer, process automation, microservices, strategy, technical lead, mern stack, cloud computing, cloud-native, scaled, system design, mongodb, responsive design, node.js, kafka, web development, security, scalability, intelligent agents, cloud architectures, mern, full-stack development, ci/cd pipelines, developer, process, infrastructures, deployment, stack, event-driven, azure, innovative solutions, typescript, production, generative ai, react, custom ai, ai-driven automation, technical strategy, llm, optical character recognition (ocr), innovation, integration, scalable ai, prisma, optima, collaborating, infrastructure, ci/cd, cross-functional teams, complex decision-making, impact analysis, flask, multi-agent, senior software engineer, deno, lambda, technical skills, product leadership, uis, decision-making, advanced ai, cross-functional initiatives, backend, automation pipelines, teams,",
