                    "## Experience  \n### Master Thesis Student at Fraunhofer Institute for Production Technology IPT (2025-08-01 – 2026-02-01)\n**Specialist**  \nConducted research on “Implementation and Comparative Evaluation of a Security Testing Framework for Cloud-Native Industrial Microservices in Bare-Metal Kubernetes Environments.” The research investigated how DevSecOps pipelines can automate security validation across both build-time and runtime stages in Kubernetes-based cloud-native systems. Key Implementation Areas • Designed a CI/CD security validation pipeline using GitLab CI/CD • Implemented static code and container security analysis using SonarQube and Trivy • Performed runtime Kubernetes security validation using kube-hunter and OWASP ZAP • Conducted network exposure testing using Nmap • Validated Kubernetes network segmentation policies using Calico NetworkPolicies • Implemented observability and runtime monitoring using Prometheus and Grafana The evaluation results were interpreted using IEC 62443 industrial cybersecurity requirements and MITRE ATT&CK tactics to understand potential attack surfaces in Kubernetes environments. This work demonstrates how DevSecOps pipelines can provide structured security validation and evidence-based security assessment for cloud-native deployments. Technologies: GitLab CI/CD • Kubernetes • Docker • SonarQube • Trivy • OWASP ZAP • kube-hunter • Nmap • Calico • Prometheus • Grafana Security Standards & Frameworks: IEC 62443 • MITRE ATT&CK\n### DevOps & Cloud (Student Assistant) at Fraunhofer Institute for Production Technology IPT · Aachen, North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany (2024-06-01 – 2026-03-01)\n• Delivered a performance comparison between GitOps (GitLab + ArgoCD) and Jenkins pipelines, achieving 45.36% faster CI/CD. • Improved pipeline performance by optimizing base images (Node.js 20-alpine). • Implemented monitoring with Prometheus and Grafana for real-time resource tracking. • Defined GitOps best practices to improve scalability and automation in Kubernetes.\nproject management, construction, microsoft, runtime security, automated testing, connectivity, segmentation, terraform, utilization, communication systems, across, testing framework, tactics, infrastructure operations, mitre att&ck, operational efficiency, issue resolution, kubernetes clusters, service, devops engineer, management, gnu make, observability, requirements management, selenium, security validation, data, analysis, hashicorp, account provisioning, vulnerability testing, devops, streamlining, cloud-native, l1 support, reliability, selenium automation, network segmentation, ci/cd security, frameworks, bash, devops & cloud, communication, automation, dashboards, docker, evidence-based practice, aws certified, aws certified solutions architect, systems management, deployment, kubernetes, research implementation, operational automation, implementation projects, endpoint security, python, room, terraform, ansible, sla, container security, cybersecurity, security analysis, boosting, support engineer, backend, intune, ci/cd pipeline, policy enforcement, ansible, validation, ci/cd, enforcement, autopilot, teams, active directory, scalability, vulnerability, gitlab, assessment, architectures, itsm, javascript, windows, standards, policy, troubleshooting, process, comparative study, helm charts, execution, calico, python selenium, av support, infrastructure deployment, pipeline management, bare-metal, microservices, operations management, linux, research, framework,",
